Package: MuscleTernary
Type: Package
Title: Work with Muscle Resultants and XFiber Data in Ternary Space
Version: 0.26
Author: Kevin M. Middleton [aut, cre] (<https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4704-1064>),
    Evan Alger-Meyer [ctb],
    Kaleb C. Sellers [ctb] (<https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3588-9562>),
    Christopher M. Zobek [ctb] (<https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1482-0726>)
Maintainer: Kevin M. Middleton <middletonk@missouri.edu>
Description: Provides tools for visualizing 3D muscle vectors in ternary
    space. Functions are available to read in origin and insertion data
    from files, with force or moment data and an arbitrary number of
    categorical or continuous variables. Plotting is accomplished via
    extensions of the 'ggtern' package.
License: GPL-2
URL: https://github.com/Middleton-Lab/MuscleTernary
BugReports: https://github.com/Middleton-Lab/MuscleTernary/issues
LazyData: TRUE
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    dplyr,
    ggplot2,
    ggtern,
    glue,
    grid,
    purrr,
    readr,
    readxl,
    rgl,
    rlang,
    stringr,
    tibble,
    tidyr,
    xml2
Encoding: UTF-8
Suggests:
    animation,
